    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1031">

                <pb facs="1199" n="1003" xml:id="pg1003"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/7–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1031<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1031-f1"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-24">24 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Tripartite Conference, Babelsberg, top secret from Winant serial number 44360. Sent the Secretary
                    Babelsberg top secret from Winant and to
                        Dept as 7434, July 24, <hi rendition="#small-caps">Comea</hi> 340.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>EAC met last night to complete two outstanding
                    documents. British informed U. S. they did not have full authority to accept
                    Soviet draft final paragraph for covering report to EAC agreement amending agreement on zones occupation
                        Germany.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1031-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1031-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1031-f1-content">
                <p>For the other portions of this message, see <ref target="#d1037">document No.
                        1037</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1031-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1031-f2-content">
                <p>For Byrnes’ reply to this message,
                    following a conversation at the Berlin Conference between Mosely and Strang, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg407">p. 407</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
